From e31161e27946e82912da7d37a490ff4036abd779 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:20:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firewall: replace the Status chain dump with a posture
 summary

Owner report: the Status page is "WAY too busy - most won't even know how to
read it and use it".

It was rendering `iptables -nvxL` AND `ip6tables -nvxL` in full - every chain as
a card, every rule as a pkts/bytes/target/prot/in/out/src/dst row. On a live box
that is 40-odd chains and several hundred rows of raw netfilter, re-fetched every
10 seconds by the auto-refresh. It was a packet-filter debugger wearing the name
of a status page: unreadable without prior iptables knowledge, and the chain text
dwarfed everything actually useful on the page.

Status now answers "what is switched on, and how is it set". Five groups:

  Core          firewall, DoS, WAN ping, WAN->LAN filter, IPv6 firewall, logging
  Rules engine  engine state, rule/object/group/service/zone/policy counts,
                commit-confirm window, armed state, last error
  Companions    Gatekeeper, Warden (+ countries, direction, logging)
  Filters       network services (mode + count), URL, keyword
  Exposure      NAT, port forwards, port triggering, DMZ, UPnP (+ pinholes,
                port protection, advertised IGD version), remote web admin
                port, SSH from WAN

The exposure group is the part a non-expert actually needs: it answers "what of
mine is reachable from the internet right now". That information was technically
present in the chain dump before, and functionally unreachable.

The CGI no longer shells out to iptables at all - both popen() calls and their
98 KB / 64 KB buffers are gone from action=status, which also makes the 10s
auto-refresh cheap. Counts are computed server-side (fw_list_count) rather than
shipping the rulelists to the browser. Raw chains remain available over the
shell for anyone who wants them; nothing else consumed that payload.

RFW_167..RFW_203 seeded English into all 25 packs, lockstep at 6519 lines. The
tokens the chain view used (RFW_12/13/14/15/16, 25-31, 39/40) are now unreferenced
but INTENTIONALLY LEFT IN PLACE - dict indices are line-based, so removing a line
renumbers every token after it.

Verified without a build: all 181 page tokens resolve against EN.dict (the
token-first trap that bit this page during Phase 1); reaper_langcheck 0 breakers;
all 25 inline script blocks parse under node in all 25 languages with 0
unresolved tokens; ASCII-clean; no dead references to the removed renderer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
